menu "ESP32 Internet radio to A2DP source"

config APP_STATION_URL
    string "Radio station stream URL (factory default)"
    default "https://coolism-web.cdn.byteark.com/;stream/1"
    help
        Direct MP3 stream URL (http:// or https://). Playlists, HLS and AAC
        streams are not supported.

        This is only the factory default: the URL can be changed at runtime
        from the web page stored in NVS, which overrides this value.

config APP_STATION_NAME
    string "Station name shown on the web page"
    default "COOLfahrenheit"
    help
        Free text, used for logging and in the config page header.

config APP_WIFI_SSID
    string "Wi-Fi network to join (factory default)"
    default ""
    help
        SSID of the access point the board uses to reach the station. Leave
        empty to boot straight into the setup access point.

        This is only the factory default: the network can be changed at
        runtime from the config web page.

config APP_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "Wi-Fi password (factory default)"
    default ""

config APP_WIFI_JOIN_TIMEOUT_S
    int "Raise the setup access point after this many seconds without Wi-Fi"
    default 25
    range 5 300
    help
        While the board cannot join the configured network the config page is
        unreachable, so after this long the board also starts its own access
        point (SSID ESP32-Radio-Setup) and keeps retrying the configured
        network in the background.

config APP_AUDIO_BUFFER_MS
    int "Jitter buffer size (ms)"
    default 1000
    range 200 3000
    help
        Decoded PCM kept between the MP3 decoder and the Bluetooth stack.
        Internet streams arrive in bursts and the Wi-Fi/Bluetooth radio
        sharing adds gaps, so this buffer is what keeps the audio continuous.
        Larger values survive longer dropouts but delay the audio.

config APP_BT_DEVICE_NAME
    string "Local Bluetooth name"
    default "ESP32-Radio-A2DP"
    help
        Name advertised by this board over Bluetooth Classic.

config APP_BT_TARGET_NAME
    string "Bluetooth speaker name to connect to"
    default ""
    help
        The A2DP source connects to the first discovered device whose name
        starts with this string. Leave empty to connect to the first
        discoverable A2DP sink.

config APP_BT_PIN_CODE
    string "Legacy pairing PIN code (1-16 digits)"
    default "1234"
    help
        PIN code this board answers with when the sink asks for a legacy
        pairing code. Many car head units expect "0000".

        Only the factory default: the value can be changed at runtime from
        the web page. Leave empty to keep the A2DP library default.

config APP_INITIAL_VOLUME
    int "Volume set when the speaker starts playing (0-127)"
    default 60
    range 0 127
    help
        A2DP volume pushed to the speaker as soon as the audio stream starts.
        Speakers come back at their own (usually maximum) level on every power
        cycle, which is what this value exists to stop.

        127 is the maximum, 0 is silent. Only the factory default: the level
        can be changed at runtime from the web page.

config APP_BT_SSP
    bool "Use Secure Simple Pairing (SSP)"
    default n
    help
        Enable Bluetooth Secure Simple Pairing for speakers that reject the
        legacy PIN handshake. This board has no display and no keypad, so the
        numeric comparison value is accepted automatically.

        Leave this off for older speakers that only support legacy pairing.

config APP_STATS_INTERVAL_MS
    int "Status log interval (ms)"
    default 5000
    range 1000 60000

endmenu
